{"tactics":[
{"id":"GAP-027:proposal:1","gap_id":"GAP-027","name":"Frailty-stratified HTA-grade PRO module within the Velmara registry","type":"registry","evidence_question":"What are the changes in health-related quality of life and symptoms at 12 weeks (primary), and the 12-month quality-of-life, utility and caregiver-burden outcomes (secondary, for CEA inputs), in frail patients starting Velmara in routine care, measured with HTA-accepted instruments?","rationale":"The registry (TAC-021) collects PROs but does not target frail patients. A frailty-stratified module with preference-based and cancer-specific instruments gives Velmara-specific frail-patient QoL and utility data for HTA and CEA use. Revised: the primary endpoint is now fixed at 12 weeks with 12-month outcomes as secondary, and a single frailty rule replaces the 'and/or' definition.","proposal_kind":"expansion","target_tactic_id":"TAC-021","expansion_scope":{"name":"Frailty-stratified HTA-grade PRO module within the Velmara registry","evidence_question":"What are the changes in health-related quality of life and symptoms at 12 weeks (primary), and the 12-month quality-of-life, utility and caregiver-burden outcomes (secondary, for CEA inputs), in frail patients starting Velmara in routine care, measured with HTA-accepted instruments?","population":"Adults with EGFR-mutant NSCLC starting Velmara in routine care who screen positive on the G8 (score of 14 or less) and are confirmed frail by baseline geriatric assessment (impairment in at least 2 of 6 domains: ADL, IADL, mobility, cognition, nutrition, comorbidity); target about 150 confirmed-frail patients across US and EU5 sites. Reference group: registry patients with G8 above 14 (non-frail). Screen-positive patients not confirmed by geriatric assessment are reported separately and excluded from the primary frail analysis. ECOG PS is recorded as a covariate and is not part of the frailty definition.","outcomes":"Primary: change from baseline in EQ-5D-5L utility and EORTC QLQ-C30 global health status at 12 weeks. Secondary: 12-month change in EQ-5D-5L and QLQ-C30 (retained for CEA utility inputs), EORTC QLQ-LC13 symptoms, time to deterioration, EQ-5D-5L utilities by progression status, caregiver burden (EQ-5D proxy and Zarit short form), treatment discontinuation and geriatric assessment change","geography":"US and EU5 (registry sites, with deliberate inclusion of community sites)","data_cut":"Interim cut when the last frail patient reaches 12 weeks (primary endpoint, about 15 months after start); final cut at 12-month follow-up of the last frail patient (about 24 months after start)","analysis":"Descriptive and mixed-model repeated-measures analysis of PRO change from baseline. Frail vs non-frail comparison is descriptive and internal only, adjusted for age, sex, ECOG, line of therapy and CNS involvement. Utility estimates by health state prepared for HTA and CEA use. Missing-data sensitivity analyses (multiple imputation, pattern-mixture).","instrument":"EQ-5D-5L, EORTC QLQ-C30, EORTC QLQ-LC13, G8 screening tool followed by geriatric assessment, caregiver EQ-5D proxy and Zarit short form, administered electronically or on paper at baseline, 4, 8 and 12 weeks and then every 12 weeks","study_design":"Prospective nested frailty-stratified cohort within the multinational observational registry. Patients are screened with the G8 at enrolment and frailty is confirmed by geriatric assessment under a single fixed rule. PRO collection is aligned to routine visits. The comparison is internal (frail vs non-frail Velmara patients); there is no external active comparator.","gap_coverage":"Closes the missing Velmara-specific, frail-targeted, HTA-grade PRO and utility evidence. Gives no frail-patient comparison against other therapies; the frail vs non-frail contrast is descriptive only.","cost_effort":"Incremental to the registry: added instruments, a G8 screen plus geriatric assessment, site training and a larger frail-patient target. Low 